                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I'm a drummer of over 20 years and the fact that I have to go through 'fun' mode to unlock any kind of decent difficulty is just annoying to start with. \n\nBut the real deal-breaker is the delay between swinging your arm to hit the snare and the game registering that you've hit the snare. It's so large that it just puts you off straight away. Even though I'm playing it perfectly in time the game thinks I'm too late and it breaks my combo.\n\nThen when it wants you to play a roll or a fill the whole thing just sounds like a muddied mess that's completely out of time with the song.\n\nI've read they've reduced the delay with v1.1,  I hate to think what it was like before but this is still not playable. \n\nSuch a shame, i was really looking forward to a good drumming game in vr so I can keep myself limber.\n\nMaybe in 6 months I'll try again...",
